ad is not shown passing its required check.","next_step":"Run or obtain the required unit check bound to head SHA 2222222.","evidence":["G05-E1"]},{"id":"G06","verdict":"CONTRADICTED","analysis":"The policy requires an approval bound exactly to the current head SHA bbbbbbb. The supplied APPROVED review is bound to aaaaaaa, the parent commit, so it does not satisfy the stated rule for this head.","next_step":"Request or obtain an independent approval review bound to SHA bbbbbbb.","evidence":["G06-E1"]},{"id":"G07","verdict":"CONTRADICTED","analysis":"The ordered commits enable the cache and then revert that change. At tip c2, the current file sets CACHE_ENABLED to False, so the cache is not enabled at the final branch tip.","next_step":"Check the effective configuration at the intended deployment target if runtime enablement is the concern.","evidence":["G07-E1"]},{"id":"G08","verdict":"CONTRADICTED","analysis":"Local main and origin/main each have one unique commit after their shared ancestor A. The clean worktree does not make the update a fast-forward or show that local commits can be discarded without preservation.","next_step":"Inspect the two unique commits and choose a preservation method before updating local main.","evidence":["G08-E1"]},{"id":"G09","verdict":"CONTRADICTED","analysis":"With attempts starting at 0 and max_retries equal to 0, the changed condition attempt <= max_retries evaluates true, allowing a retry. The diff therefore contradicts the commit message’s promise; no tests were changed, and no test run is evidenced.","next_step":"Correct the boundary condition and verify the zero-retry case against the stated call contract.","evidence":["G09-E1"]},{"id":"G10","verdict":"UNKNOWN","analysis":"The listing is incomplete: only 100 of 130 changed files were returned, the next page failed with 503, and review inventory was not fetched. The displayed examples cannot establish whether undisplayed files or reviews contain blockers.","next_step":"Fetch the remaining changed-file pages and review inventory, then assess their contents.","evidence":["G10-E1"]},{"id":"G11","verdict":"CONTRADICTED","analysis":"The PRs touch different files but change opposite sides of a shared message contract: the producer emits version 2 with payload, while the consumer expects version 1 and reads value. The fixture says producer output feeds consumer input and integration results are absent, so path non-overlap alone cannot establish compatibility.","next_step":"Run an integration check of the producer-consumer pair against the deployed message contract before treating them as compatible.","evidence":["G11-E1"]},{"id":"G12","verdict":"UNKNOWN","analysis":"The PR is merged, but the complete GitHub deployment-record inventory is empty and no release tag is present. That does not establish production deployment, since external deployment systems are outside the observed inventory.","next_step":"Check the authoritative production deployment system for this merge commit or its release artifact.","evidence":["G12-E1"]}],"limitations":["Evidence is limited to the supplied snapshots and excerpts, frozen at their recorded times; it does not establish later state.","A displayed diff or changed test file does not prove tests ran, and a merged PR does not prove deployment."]}
